review_comments.body:
The width guarantee at `tools/cpp/duckdb_cpp.hpp:2115` is not enforced: `BuildDecimal` limits storage tiers, leaving INT128 unchecked. The typed API already behaved this way; this PR adds the promise. `Value::CreateDecimal(factory, int128_t {10000, 0}, 4, 0)` prints `10000`; binding fails with `Serialization Error: Failed to deserialize value: value is not valid for type DECIMAL(4,0)`. `Value::CreateDecimal(factory, int128_t {0, INT64_MIN}, 38, 0)` asserts in `ToText()` (`cast_helpers.cpp:213`, `value > NumericLimits<hugeint_t>::Minimum()`). I would replace tier limits after width/scale validation with this width check and update `src/include/duckdb_v2.h:16678` (“is not range-checked against the width”), or remove the promise.

```cpp
	auto value = Convert(in_value);
	if (value >= Hugeint::POWERS_OF_TEN[width] || value <= -Hugeint::POWERS_OF_TEN[width]) {
		throw InvalidInputException("value does not fit the declared DECIMAL width");
	}
	if (width > Decimal::MAX_WIDTH_INT64) {
		return Value::DECIMAL(value, width, scale);
	}
	return Value::DECIMAL(Hugeint::Cast<int64_t>(value), width, scale);
```

